course: dictionary
lesson: 8695
title: Selfish and what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Selfish describes someone who thinks mostly about themselves and what they want, and does not care enough about other people. It is an adjective, so it describes a person or an act: a selfish person, a selfish act. Its forms are selfish, more selfish and most selfish.
explain: Context helps here. «I'll take you through all the Courts!» The word roadhog appears in this text, and the notes tell us a roadhog is a selfish, dangerous driver. The clues about the road and danger show that selfish can mean caring only about getting where you want, even when it puts others at risk.
explain: «Just a pig—a plain pig!» Pig is not about a farm animal here. The words just and plain show the speaker is calling someone names. Pig means a selfish, thoughtless person, so the speaker is saying the person is thinking only of themselves.
explain: Stories and lessons show selfishness as wrong. The selfish giant would not share his garden, and pupils learn that sharing and taking turns are the opposite. Look for phrases such as «selfish behaviour», «a selfish giant» and «don't be selfish». Try your meaning in the sentence: if «a selfish giant» means a giant who thinks only of himself, the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Selfish means thinking mostly about yourself and what you want.
fact: A selfish act is done only for your own good, at other people's expense.
fact: Sharing and taking turns are the opposite of being selfish.
fact: A roadhog is a selfish, dangerous driver.
fact: Pig can mean a selfish, thoughtless person, as in «Just a pig—a plain pig!»
exercise: «The selfish giant would not share his garden.» What does selfish mean here? | Sad and lonely | *Thinking only of himself and not caring about others | Kind to the children | Very large and green
exercise: In «Just a pig—a plain pig!», what does pig mean? | A small dog | A farm animal | A kind neighbour | *A selfish, thoughtless person
exercise: Which is a selfish act? | He shared his sweets with his friends | He helped carry the shopping | *He ate all the sweets and gave none to his sister | He said sorry for breaking the toy
test: Which sentence shows selfish behaviour? | He let his little brother go first on the slide | *He grabbed the last biscuit before anyone else could take one | He waited his turn patiently | He picked up litter in the park
test: Which word is the closest opposite of selfish? | Tall | *Generous | Lazy | Loud
exam: Ayo says «selfish» means very tall. What does it really mean? | *Thinking mostly about yourself and not caring enough about others | Very quiet and shy | Very tall and strong | Quick at running
